Give a method a mutable receiver when it needs to change a field.
For example, a new round can reset a player's score.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Player = | name String, score I32 = 0 |

    reset_score |this ~Player| {
        ~this.score = 0
    }

    player ~= Player("Priya", score = 10)
    ~player.reset_score()
]

The declaration gives `this` permission to write. The caller creates a
mutable binding with `~=` and grants the method exclusive access by writing
`~` before `player` at the call. When the method returns, the same player's
score reads zero.
